From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:18:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: f_mass_storage: honour UMS_ABORT_KEYED while
 idle

While the host does not send commands the gadget only checks for Ctrl+C,
so with UMS_ABORT_KEYED the documented 'any key' only worked between
transfers. Phones have no Ctrl+C key.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c
index 76ee08dc..fa7b7408 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_mass_storage.c
@@ -673,6 +673,12 @@ static int sleep_thread(struct fsg_common *common)
 			if (ctrlc())
 				return -EPIPE;
 
+			/* Any key ends it too, phones have no Ctrl+C */
+			if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CMD_UMS_ABORT_KEYED) && tstc()) {
+				getchar();
+				return -EPIPE;
+			}
+
 			/* Check cable connection */
 			if (!g_dnl_board_usb_cable_connected())
 				return -EIO;
